// Pegasus's shared core: the part of the program a browser and a server both run, so the world's rules stay one program.
// Sim (the zone's simulation, in the whole, client and server roles), the Loader (the catalog, the content keys and the
// worker pool; a server's builds only what Sim needs), connected play (netplay, partsync), the world's image and its fetch,
// the messages between the actors, and the driven checks of those. It holds no window, GPU, SDL, Render, Player or Audio:
// `pegasus` (the browser) and `pegasusserver` (`pegasus-server`) each add their own actors and a shell.
//
// Sim and the Loader send to a display and a sound by the actor traits below, not by the browser's actors: Render and
// Audio meet them by their behaviours (an actor conforms by having them), and a server's stand-in does too.

mod pegasuscore;

